ethercat (1.7.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Consume two SII words per read, as 1.6.9 did. Advancing by a 4-word
    reply skipped EEPROM words, so the first scan stored no identity and
    the slave stayed INIT E 0x00000000:0x00000000 until reboot.
  * Retry a scan that finishes without a vendor id instead of latching
    error_flag.
  * Keep the in-flight datagram when a slave FSM is still waiting, so the
    ring does not recycle the slot and each lost reply does not cost the
    full IO timeout.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:50:00 -0400

ethercat (1.7.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Replace and provide ethercat-master / etherlabmaster so the tools
    package installs over the IgH packages without a file conflict and
    still satisfies linuxcnc-ethercat.
  * Declare the autoconf tools the DKMS build actually runs.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 03:20:00 -0400

ethercat (1.7.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Read 14 bytes of SII data when the slave returns 4 words.
    The 1.7 merge kept the 10-byte fetch, so mailbox configuration and
    PDO mapping were built from a truncated EEPROM image.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 03:12:00 -0400

ethercat (1.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rebase on official stable-1.7 (SII cache, PDO mode, ioctl 43).
  * Keep parallel per-slave scan/config and AL recovery from 1.6.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:50:00 -0400

ethercat (1.6.13) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sync official stable-1.6 through 1.6.13 (drivers, FoE/EoE hardening,
    datagram re-order barriers, max-frame split).
  * Keep our parallel slave scan/config, AL recovery and DC patches.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:40:00 -0400

ethercat (1.6.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Parallel slave configuration (multi-slave bus reaches OP in seconds).
  * SDO information API and bus rescan in the realtime library.
  * Numerous stability fixes (datagram index reuse, external-ring timing,
    mailbox state machines, SDO dictionary gating, DC sync1 shift).
  * SII timing relaxed for slow EEPROMs.
  * New ethercat diag command, slave port bypass detection and upstream
    port inference.
  * FoE password support.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
